Architecture rules:
- lib/data/ is the Brain. It must not import lib/features/.
- lib/features/ is UI only. Durable state and PocketBase I/O belong in lib/data/.
- database_service.dart is the Brain root; domain logic lives in part files.
- PocketBase system ids are 15-char strings. Do not use business IDs in REST paths or relation payloads that require system IDs.
- UI mutations must be optimistic: update local Brain cache first, notify UI, then sync PocketBase in background.
- Do not introduce full refetch fan-out after small mutations unless unavoidable.
- Date + time picking must use the Omni-Picker.
- Do not rewrite architecture when fixing local bugs.
- Treat `build()` cost, offscreen-page work, periodic rebuilds, and repeated projections as correctness concerns, not optional optimization.
